<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nordgau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bavarian Nordgau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nordgau, or Bavarian Nordgau, was a medieval frontier region north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, roughly corresponding to the later Upper Palatinate and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>. It was ruled by margraves in the 10th and 11th centuries. By the Treaty of Pavia in 1329 its northern part went to the Palatine line of the Wittelsbachs and became the Upper Palatinate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nordgau.jpg" alt="Nordgau" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alphathon /ˈæɫfə.θɒn · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nordgau_locator_map_(1000).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
